{"title":"Career roadmap · Ship Designer","role":"Ship Designer","summary":"A Ship Designer develops the technical design of ships, vessels and offshore structures. The work combines naval architecture, hydrodynamics, ship structures, stability, propulsion, marine systems, CAD/CAE, production engineering and safety regulations.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Naval Architecture & Ship Building"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for Naval Architecture & Ship Building graduates."},{"type":"p","text":"A Ship Designer may work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Commercial ships"},{"text":"Naval vessels"},{"text":"Offshore vessels"},{"text":"Tankers"},{"text":"Bulk carriers"},{"text":"Container ships"},{"text":"Ferries"},{"text":"Tugboats"},{"text":"Workboats"},{"text":"Fishing vessels"},{"text":"High-speed craft"},{"text":"Autonomous/smart vessels"},{"text":"Subsea and offshore structures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Typical design flow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Owner Requirement","Concept Design","Hull Design","Hydrostatics","Stability","Resistance/Propulsion","Structural Design","Systems","3D Model","Production Drawings","Classification","Construction"]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Starts","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"note","label":"Current degree","text":"B.Tech / B.E. Naval Architecture & Ship Building"},{"type":"note","label":"Desired career","text":"Ship Designer"},{"type":"flow","items":["Naval Architecture","Ship Design","Marine Engineering","Shipbuilding"],"label":"Career cluster"},{"type":"note","label":"Entry accessibility","text":"Direct"},{"type":"note","label":"Typical entry titles","text":"Graduate Engineer Trainee, Junior Naval Architect, Ship Design Engineer, Naval Architect, Hull Design Engineer, Marine Design Engineer"},{"type":"note","label":"